//! Literal translation of soothe3's reference gain path (in progress).
//!
//! This module is the reference side of the differential check: plain Rust over
//! slices, translated from the restored binary (`/tmp/opencode/rea/soothe3-restored.bin`,
//! image base `0x180000000`). Each function's doc comment cites its address, and the
//! arithmetic keeps the order and float width the binary uses. Evidence for each
//! translation is a fixture generated by emulating the binary in
//! `tools/smooth-core/research/re-tools/emulate/` (`reference_magnitude_fixture.py`).
//!
//! Status, per function:
//!
//! | address    | function                     | state                                   |
//! |------------|------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
//! | `0x6181b0` | complex magnitude kernel     | translated; power stage bit-exact, IPP sqrt tail modelled (`magnitude.rs`) |
//! | `0x8e04c0` | gain helper body (entry; `0x8e0858` is an interior label, body ~17.5 KB) | **not translated**; entry, caller chain (section 19), field layout (`gain_layout.rs`, section 20) and CFG (`gain_body_cfg.json`) mapped |
//!
//! The gain body is entered at `0x8e04c0` (not `0x8e0858`, which is an interior label
//! of the same function). It is entered four times per block via the chain
//! `0x8d98a0` -> `0x8e04c0`, calls the magnitude kernel eight times (`0x8e13a8`), and
//! calls `logf`, `powf` and `expf`. It is not yet translated: about 17.5 KB of code, a
//! stack frame of `0x4ae8` bytes, and the state fields it reads are not yet mapped.
//!
//! Planned public API (not defined yet, so nothing here is wired into `dsp.rs`):
//! per-block input of magnitude frames and parameters (depth, sharpness, selectivity,
//! band records, attack/release, focus, soft/hard mode), output of a per-bin gain
//! curve, with all state in a struct allocated at reset.

pub mod gain;
pub mod gain_layout;
pub mod magnitude;
